---
import BaseLayout from '@/components/layout/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Legendary Resistance" active="play"
  ><header class="page-hero">
    <div class="site-shell">
      <p class="kicker">Boss fight</p><h1>Choose a resistance plan</h1><p>
        One isolated premium save spell is not a plan. Choose how the party will
        change the encounter even if the boss negates a failed save.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header><section class="section section--first">
    <div class="site-shell">
      <div class="reference-card-grid">
        <article class="tool-panel">
          <h2>Bypass</h2><p>
            Use no-save encounter splitting, terrain, buffs or map control when
            the effect and geometry are legal. Check exact wording rather than
            assuming that a famous spell bypasses every defense.
          </p><a href="/spells/?save=none">Spells with no indexed save →</a>
        </article>
        <article class="tool-panel">
          <h2>Burn intentionally</h2><p>
            Coordinate save pressure with allies and preserve a follow-up.
            Decide what the party gains if the boss spends resistance; avoid
            spending alone without a second threat.
          </p><a href="/quick/party/">Coordinate party roles →</a>
        </article>
        <article class="tool-panel">
          <h2>Ignore temporarily</h2><p>
            Isolate support, remove minion actions, deny escape or secure the
            objective. The largest creature is not automatically the
            highest-value target.
          </p><a href="/quick/objectives/">Play the objective →</a>
        </article>
      </div><p>
        Derived from the encounter responses in Chapter 18. The active monster
        and spell entries control immunities, targeting and resolution.
      </p><div class="form-actions">
        <a class="button" href="/chapters/18-combat-decision-engine/"
          >Combat Decision Engine</a
        ><a class="button" href="/chapters/58-worked-encounter-playbooks/"
          >Worked encounters</a
        ><a class="button" href="/prepare/">Prepare the boss package</a><a
          class="button"
          href="/quick/targeting/">Targeting reference</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
  </section></BaseLayout
>
